    {
      "id": "msML4DjlH0crRMVi3ba4q",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 358.3265766130819,
      "y": 91.95954767796673,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 525,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3c",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1357830531,
      "version": 2289,
      "versionNonce": 420174307,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792844610848,
      "created": 1792650911978,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Memory from Hierarchical Perception: \nThe memory is not REAL memory without a progressive \"strengthening\" process.\nA person is not your friend just because you talk with each other on something\nthis day and play together that day. It's because you share something in common\nand have got a feeling about each other.\n\nFor a pet, it's playing, keeping company and having conversation (and maybe other\nthings, coming soon).\n\nThe process doesn't have to be long or tortuous but is got to be memorable (as\npun of memory-able!).\n\nThe Decay:\nLRU elimination. Recalling a memory stretches its lifespan and gives it chance to\nbe strengthened. This is a simplified model of the fact that \"you don't use it\nyou lose it\".\n\nRecall:\nSearch by calling Recall tools with/without query. The results are sorted by time\ndesc. \n- With query: ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Memory from Hierarchical Perception: \nThe memory is not REAL memory without a progressive \"strengthening\" process.\nA person is not your friend just because you talk with each other on something this day and play together that day. It's because you share something in common and have got a feeling about each other.\n\nFor a pet, it's playing, keeping company and having conversation (and maybe other things, coming soon).\n\nThe process doesn't have to be long or tortuous but is got to be memorable (as pun of memory-able!).\n\nThe Decay:\nLRU elimination. Recalling a memory stretches its lifespan and gives it chance to be strengthened. This is a simplified model of the fact that \"you don't use it you lose it\".\n\nRecall:\nSearch by calling Recall tools with/without query. The results are sorted by time desc. \n- With query: ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
