      "locked": false,
      "text": "Yes",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "47MEhTtmo7sxU27h4-sjs",
      "originalText": "Yes",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "ZQkSBD_1mzDyHOao8FH3I",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6104.884705566384,
      "y": 302.0948374084519,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 625,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6h",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1675963555,
      "version": 3080,
      "versionNonce": 2019799395,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792844610851,
      "created": 1792658096644,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Difference\n- Specifics are recorded unconditionally after every meaningful event. There's no\nchance for a specific to be missed.\n- Impressions are recorded by the LLM using tools, guided with explicit prompts,\nwhenever they think it necessary (the act of the tool call is the very sign).\n- Memories are updated when the Impressions overlap or contradict with each\nother, which is evaluated after any loop ends. Based on their old states, the\nMemories are updated to reflect the latest long-term perception of the pet and\nthe Impressions are updated to resolve the contradiction and overlapping\ncontent.\n- Specifics and Impressions are append-only, while Memories are read-write, just\nlike a\nregular text file. \n\nCommon Ground\n- They are all written in first-person as the pet itself.\n- Specifics and Impressions are eliminated when not recalled after some period of\ntime.\n\nAppend-only Consideration\nThe append-only-ness creates a space for conflicts, but ensures the \ntruthfulness of the log. The time fields of the records also enables the conflicts\nto be\nresolved logically even if there are some. Additionally, the process of elimination\nwill erase things eventually, so the conflicts are not permanent.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Difference\n- Specifics are recorded unconditionally after every meaningful event. There's no chance for a specific to be missed.\n- Impressions are recorded by the LLM using tools, guided with explicit prompts, whenever they think it necessary (the act of the tool call is the very sign).\n- Memories are updated when the Impressions overlap or contradict with each other, which is evaluated after any loop ends. Based on their old states, the Memories are updated to reflect the latest long-term perception of the pet and the Impressions are updated to resolve the contradiction and overlapping content.\n- Specifics and Impressions are append-only, while Memories are read-write, just like a\nregular text file. \n\nCommon Ground\n- They are all written in first-person as the pet itself.\n- Specifics and Impressions are eliminated when not recalled after some period of time.\n\nAppend-only Consideration\nThe append-only-ness creates a space for conflicts, but ensures the \ntruthfulness of the log. The time fields of the records also enables the conflicts to be\nresolved logically even if there are some. Additionally, the process of elimination will erase things eventually, so the conflicts are not permanent.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
